    "Answer": "Straight-line with positive slope", "Image": "",
    "Explaination": "Total iron loss Pi = hysteresis loss (Wh = η·Bm^1.6·f) + eddy loss (We = ke·Bm²·f²·t²·V). Dividing by f: Pi/f = Wh_const + (eddy coefficient)·f, which is of the form y = c + mf. Hence Pi/f versus f is a straight line with positive slope. This is the standard method of separating hysteresis and eddy current losses."
